  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is Theorem 2.11 part (2) in the exactly isothermal pressure branch P(rho)=kappa*rho, kappa>0, for the exact global rescaled weak-solution definition and bounded pseudo-energy plus finite dissipation assumptions. It concludes weak L1 convergence to the mass-normalized Gaussian. The complete author body retains all local rescaling, ODE asymptotics, entropy/tightness, slow-time compactness, stress disappearance and Fokker--Planck identification arguments. The named entropy convergence result is retained as a published prerequisite; non-isothermal, existence/compactness and other asymptotic assertions are unselected context.",
